<section id="process" class="py-16 bg-gray-100">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-gray-900 mb-8 text-center">
      How to Commission a Pet Portrait
    </h2>
    <div class="mx-auto">
      <ol class="space-y-8 list-none">
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 mr-4 rounded-full bg-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xl">1</div>
          <div class="text-left">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Initial Contact</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              Send me an email at <a href="mailto:book@melmartins.art" class="text-blue-600 underline">commission@melmartins.art</a> including the size,
              medium (colored pencils or charcoal) and any other requests you may
              have. Keep in mind that the bigger the artwork, the more details
              I'll be able to include (but I will work to get the full impact even
              on a smaller scale).
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 mr-4 rounded-full bg-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xl">2</div>
          <div class="text-left">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Consultation & Planning</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              We will discuss via email everything about the artwork you're
              commissioning to make sure the final result will be your pet
              brought to life on paper. At this point I'll request photo
              references of your pet. Ideally clear, well-lit and high resolution
              images are best, but I will do my best to work with what you have
              available and still deliver good results. We will talk about the
              composition, whether to include a favorite toy or a background, etc.
              I will also let you know how much time I will need to conclude the
              portrait.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 mr-4 rounded-full bg-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xl">3</div>
          <div class="text-left">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Payment & Confirmation</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              Once we've agreed on all the details, I'll send you a payment request for 20% of the total price to secure your spot in my queue.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 mr-4 rounded-full bg-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xl">4</div>
          <div class="text-left">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Creation & Updates</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              The wait! I understand this part can be tough and I'll do my best to send you updates.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 mr-4 rounded-full bg-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xl">5</div>
          <div class="text-left">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Delivery</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              If you're local to me (I live in Bloomington, MN), we can agree on a pick up location. If not, I will mail your artwork to you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
